{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's own numbers cannot clear the policy gate. Against the booked optimal route of 12.0 km, the trace's 14.39 km is an excess of 2.39 km — 19.92% of optimal, which is NOT greater than the 20% POL-RD-01 requires. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH greater than 20% of optimal_distance_km AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms; the percentage limb fails, so no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. A 2.39 km variation is exactly the ordinary lane change, forced U-turn or short gantry-avoidance distance that the single numeric gate in POL-RD-01 exists to keep out of refundable disputes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02841", "EV-TRIP-02841"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace governs this measurement, and both distance fields fail. POL-RD-01 provides that where gps_trace.trace_distance_km and trip_record.actual_distance_km disagree, the trace figure governs and the trip_record copy may not be cited for the threshold test. The trace records 14.39 km, an excess of 19.92%. Even the rounded trip_record convenience copy of 14.4 km yields an excess of exactly 2.40 km, i.e. exactly 20.0% of 12.0 km — still not GREATER than 20%. Reading the larger field does not save the claim; reading the governing field defeats it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02841", "EV-TRIP-02841"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The variation is not merely unestablished, it is nowhere near MATERIAL. POL-RD-01 makes an excess additional MATERIAL only above 50% of optimal or above 8.0 km absolute; the measured 2.39 km is under a third of that absolute figure, so the driver_profile check mandated by POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) is available. Were that check run, the citable counters disclose no repeat pattern: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 196, a ratio of zero.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02841", "EV-GPS-02841", "EV-TRIP-02841"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden and has not discharged it. POL-RD-08 requires the rider to show, citing evidence IDs, an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold measured from an unimpaired gps_trace. The undisputed record shows 14.39 km against a 12.0 km optimal — 19.92% — which falls short of the gate. The burden therefore never shifts to the driver, and no exculpatory clause needs to be reached to decide this case.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02841", "EV-TRIP-02841"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No clause moves the baseline against which the rider is measuring. The vehicle type is RYDE_X, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary basis for pooled trips does not apply and the booked 12.0 km is the correct optimal; pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run and no amended optimal exists on the record; and the chat log carries zero messages, so POL-RD-04 has no rider instruction to act on and its corroboration test cannot be met. The comparison the rider himself makes — 14.39 km against 12.0 km — is therefore the correct comparison, and it fails.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02841", "EV-CHAT-02841"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace the rider relies on is complete and unimpaired for policy purposes. It carries 113 fixes at a 10 s sampling interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, and a maximum gap of 0 seconds, so it meets none of the impairment limbs POL-RD-07(a) to (c) sets. Its 14.39 km measurement is reliable exactly as recorded; there is no data failure of the kind that would force escalation under POL-RD-10 on the trace's account, and the arithmetic on which this defence rests is sound.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02841"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The one refund route that survives a finding of no deviation yields nothing here. POL-RD-09(4) refunds a charge line for a gantry the trace never passes, or an airport surcharge on a trip that does not originate at an airport, whether or not a deviation exists. On this fare breakdown the charged distance of 14.4 km is the same measurement as the 14.39 km trace and not a phantom line; the erp_lines array is empty and no gantry is charged at all; and no airport surcharge line appears on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport. There is no standalone billing-integrity correction to make.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02841", "EV-GPS-02841"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "A threshold failure is a win for the driver on this record. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION means the filing party's claim is not supported by the evidence and the present state stands: fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, and nothing in that outcome disturbs the driver's fare. The driver's contemporaneous explanation — a minor detour around a road-works sign — describes precisely the small, sub-threshold variation the gate tolerates; no exoneration clause is invoked and none is needed, because POL-RD-01 disposes of the matter at the threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02841", "EV-GPS-02841"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.92,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This dispute turns on a single numeric gate, and it decides the case. The platform's booked optimal route for this trip is 12.0 km (trip_record EV-TRIP-02841). POL-RD-01 makes the GPS trace the governing distance and expressly bars the trip_record's rounded copy from the threshold test, so the measure is the trace figure of 14.39 km (EV-GPS-02841). Excess = 14.39 - 12.0 = 2.39 km. That clears the absolute limb (greater than 0.8 km) but POL-RD-01 requires BOTH limbs to pass: the excess must also be greater than 20% of optimal, and 2.39 / 12.0 = 19.92%, which is not greater than 20%. Reading the trip_record's convenience copy of 14.4 km would give exactly 20.0%, still not greater than 20%, and POL-RD-01 forbids citing it in any event. The establishment test therefore fails and no deviation exists, 'however the rider characterises the trip'. The outcome is NO_ACTION: the fare stands as charged (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The rider's own advocate reached the same conclusion, and the driver's advocate's threshold argument is accepted on the trace figure. On the driver's explanation: his counterparty statement says only 'a minor detour because of a road works sign' and cites no advisory. The only traffic_advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02841-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and no advisory covers this corridor in this window. Under POL-RD-13 an uncited traffic excuse carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-03 is unavailable — but this point does not need to be reached, because the threshold disposes of the matter before any exoneration clause is considered, and the absence of an advisory is a gap in the bundle, not the contradiction POL-RD-10(5) escalates on. On the remaining routes: there is no amended endpoint (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null), no pooled itinerary (vehicle_type RYDE_X), and no chat instruction (EV-CHAT-02841 holds zero messages), so the booked 12.0 km optimal is the only baseline and it is the correct one; and there is no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4) — erp_lines is empty, no airport surcharge appears, and the 14.4 km charged distance is the same measurement as the 14.39 km trace, not a phantom line. No driver compensation arises because the rider was not billed for less distance than the trace records (14.4 km billed against 14.39 km traced). No referral is produced: POL-RD-06(c) is not engaged because no MATERIAL deviation was established and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 196, so no repeat pattern exists, and POL-RD-09(4) has no billing defect to refer. The deciding fact rests on the GPS trace and trip_record, each at full weight 1.0, so confidence is not discounted."
  },
